{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019zkxh2BQDf8RPFK7kZBDMq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libbase122\n2\t\n3\t`libbase122` is a C89 library for encoding and decoding [Base122](https://blog.kevinalbs.com/base122).\n4\t\n5\t`libbase122` compiles with `-std=c89`.\n6\t\n7\tThis repository includes `b122`, an application for encoding and decoding Base122.\n8\t\n9\t## Usage\n10\t\n11\tUsage of `libbase122`:\n12\t```c\n13\t#include \"base122.h\"\n14\t#include <stdio.h>\n15\t\n16\tint main(void) {\n17\t  unsigned char *data = (unsigned char *)\"\\x34\\x19\\x2d\\x46\\x63\\x3c\\x14\";\n18\t  unsigned char decoded[16] = {0};\n19\t  base122_error_t error;\n20\t  int got;\n21\t  size_t written;\n22\t\n23\t  got = base122_decode(data, 8, decoded, sizeof(decoded), &written, &error);\n24\t\n25\t  if (got == -1) {\n26\t    fprintf(stderr, \"Error decoding: %s\\n\", error.msg);\n27\t    return 1;\n28\t  }\n29\t  printf(\"Decoded the string: %s\\n\", decoded);\n30\t  return 0;\n31\t}\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\tUsage of `b122`:\n35\t```\n36\tcat example.jpg | b122 > encoded.b122\n37\tcat encoded.b122 | b122 -d > decoded.jpg\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t## Using with CMake\n41\t\n42\tCMake targets are exported. To use libbase122 in a CMake project:\n43\t\n44\t```cmake\n45\tadd_executable (app app.c)\n46\tfind_package (Base122 REQUIRED)\n47\ttarget_link_libraries (app base122::static) # Or base122::shared\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t## Contributing\n51\t\n52\tContributions are welcome.\n53\t\n54\tGitHub actions is used to compile and test each commit. See [cmake.yml](.github/workflows/cmake.yml) for the platform specific C flags.\n55\t\n56\tTests may be run locally with:\n57\t\n58\t```bash\n59\tcmake -S. -Bcmake-build\n60\tcmake --build cmake-build --target test-libbase122\n61\t./cmake-build/test-libbase122\n62\t```\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15e69459-2c03-4918-81fb-90f19cc2c0fc","uuid":"3a3828a3-1ea1-481a-b30d-ad4c3248837d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:57:31.693Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-bo8CWW/project/c_src/README.md","content":"# libbase122\n\n`libbase122` is a C89 library for encoding and decoding [Base122](https://blog.kevinalbs.com/base122).\n\n`libbase122` compiles with `-std=c89`.\n\nThis repository includes `b122`, an application for encoding and decoding Base122.\n\n## Usage\n\nUsage of `libbase122`:\n```c\n#include \"base122.h\"\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n  unsigned char *data = (unsigned char *)\"\\x34\\x19\\x2d\\x46\\x63\\x3c\\x14\";\n  unsigned char decoded[16] = {0};\n  base122_error_t error;\n  int got;\n  size_t written;\n\n  got = base122_decode(data, 8, decoded, sizeof(decoded), &written, &error);\n\n  if (got == -1) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error decoding: %s\\n\", error.msg);\n    return 1;\n  }\n  printf(\"Decoded the string: %s\\n\", decoded);\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nUsage of `b122`:\n```\ncat example.jpg | b122 > encoded.b122\ncat encoded.b122 | b122 -d > decoded.jpg\n```\n\n## Using with CMake\n\nCMake targets are exported. To use libbase122 in a CMake project:\n\n```cmake\nadd_executable (app app.c)\nfind_package (Base122 REQUIRED)\ntarget_link_libraries (app base122::static) # Or base122::shared\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome.\n\nGitHub actions is used to compile and test each commit. See [cmake.yml](.github/workflows/cmake.yml) for the platform specific C flags.\n\nTests may be run locally with:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S. -Bcmake-build\ncmake --build cmake-build --target test-libbase122\n./cmake-build/test-libbase122\n```\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
